# Mezzanine floor beam — design report

<% texl.import "basis-of-design.texl" ~> (d -> bind "bod" d.data) %>
<% texl.import "analysis.texl" ~> (d -> bind "calc" d.data) %>
| Document | Revision | Date | Prepared | Checked |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| MZ-001 | B | 2026-11-09 | Anna | Marco |
<!--{ int1 : rich }-->
## 1 Introduction

A public gallery is to be added at first floor level of an existing hall: a
steel mezzanine floor carried by simply supported beams. This report
presents the design of these beams. It is short on purpose: it summarises
the design and links to the documents that hold the details, from which it
takes its figures:

- [Basis of design](basis-of-design.texl) (MZ-002): codes, structure,
  materials, loads, load combinations and acceptance criteria.
- [Calculation note](analysis.texl) (MZ-003): method, checks of the proposed
  section and of the alternatives.

A change in one of them updates this report.
<!--{ scp1 : rich }-->
## 2 Scope of work

In scope:

- the strength and the deflection of the floor beams, for the loads of the
  basis of design;
- the choice of the lightest adequate IPE section.

Out of scope: the deck, the connections, the columns and the foundations,
the fire resistance and the dynamic response of the floor. These are
addressed in the recommendations.
<!--{ bod1 : markdown }-->
## 3 Basis of design

The design follows the Eurocodes: EN 1990, EN 1991-1-1 and EN 1993-1-1, with
their recommended values. The key data, from the
[basis of design](basis-of-design.texl):

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Structure | <% bod.beams %> simply supported beams, span <% bod.L %> m, spacing <% bod.spacing %> m |
| Steel | <% bod.steel.grade.name %>, f<sub>y</sub> = <% bod.fy %> N/mm² |
| Permanent load | g<sub>k</sub> = <% bod.gk %> kN/m, plus the self-weight of the beam |
| Variable load | q<sub>k</sub> = <% bod.qk %> kN/m, category C3 |
| ULS partial factors | γ<sub>G</sub> = <% bod.gammaG %>, γ<sub>Q</sub> = <% bod.gammaQ %> |
| Deflection limits | L / <% bod.deflection_total %> total, L / <% bod.deflection_variable %> under variable load |
<caption>Table 1: Key design data.</caption>
<!--{ mth1 : markdown }-->
## 4 Method statement

1. The loads and the combinations of the basis of design are applied to a
   simply supported beam with a uniform load.
2. The bending moment, the shear force and the deflection follow from the
   closed-form solutions of beam theory, by linear elastic analysis.
3. The proposed <% bod.section.name %> is checked for bending and shear
   (EN 1993-1-1, 6.2) and for deflection against the limits of the basis of
   design. The deck restrains the top flange, so lateral-torsional buckling
   does not govern.
4. The same checks are repeated for the IPE sections of the steel library,
   to find the lightest adequate one.

The equations and the intermediate results are in the
[calculation note](analysis.texl), sections 1 and 2.
<!--{ res1 : markdown }-->
## 5 Analysis results

<% p = calc.r %>
The proposed <% p.section.name %> carries a design load of
<% calc.fix (p.qd, 1) %> kN/m, with a midspan moment of
<% calc.fix (p.MEd, 1) %> kNm. Its checks:

| Check | Effect | Limit | Utilisation |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Bending | <% math.round p.sigma %> N/mm² | <% math.round p.fyd %> N/mm² | <% calc.pct p.u_M %> % |
| Shear | <% calc.fix (p.VEd, 1) %> kN | <% calc.fix (p.VRd, 1) %> kN | <% calc.pct p.u_V %> % |
| Total deflection | <% calc.fix (p.d, 1) %> mm | <% calc.fix (p.d_lim, 1) %> mm | <% calc.pct p.u_d %> % |
| Deflection, variable load | <% calc.fix (p.dq, 1) %> mm | <% calc.fix (p.dq_lim, 1) %> mm | <% calc.pct p.u_dq %> % |
<caption>Table 2: Checks of the proposed section.</caption>
