## 6 Conclusions

<% best = calc.lightest %>
- The proposed <% p.section.name %> is
  <% p.ok ? "**adequate**" ; "**not adequate**" %>. Its governing check is the
  <% p.governing %>, at <% calc.pct p.u %> % of the limit.
- <% (math.max (p.u_d, p.u_dq) > math.max (p.u_M, p.u_V))
    ? "Stiffness, not strength, governs the design" ; "Strength governs the design" %>:
  bending is at <% calc.pct p.u_M %> %, shear at <% calc.pct p.u_V %> %, the total
  deflection at <% calc.pct p.u_d %> % of the limit.
- The lightest adequate section is the <% best.section.name %>, at
  <% calc.pct best.u %> % (<% best.governing %>).
<!--{ rec1 : markdown }-->
## 7 Recommendations

<%
saving = (p.section.mass - best.section.mass) * bod.L * bod.beams   # kg of steel
%>
1. <% (best.section.name == p.section.name)
    ? "Keep the " + p.section.name + "."
    ; "Adopt the " + best.section.name + " instead of the " + p.section.name + ": it saves " + text.from (math.round saving) + " kg of steel over the " + text.from bod.beams + " beams." %>
2. Confirm the partial factors and the imposed load against the National
   Annex and the client's brief before issue.
3. Design the end plate connections for the end shear of
   <% calc.fix (best.VEd, 1) %> kN.
4. Check the floor for vibrations: the gallery is open to the public, and a
   lighter beam makes the floor livelier.
5. Define the fire resistance required and the protection of the beams.
